  {
    "episode_id": 78130,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78130.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "He's the leader of the party. He's the president of the United States. He's the leader of the free world. He made this decision. And he is the only person who could have made this decision. And I think one thing we've seen about Joe Biden time and time again is the humanity he displays, the humility he often displays. And he made this decision on his own. He made it I think for the same reason he decided to run in 2020 to save the soul of America. And that was, that was his purpose as a person getting out. You know, the idea that someone could have forced him out, I think is, is probably something that people are saying on Twitter, but doesn't have as much basis in reality. He made the decision to get out and that is his decision to make. Therefore now he has released his delegate. He is not the, I think people get this mixed up too. He is not the nominee right now. He people called him the presumptive nominee because even though he has one primary in state and those delegates therefore are chosen to vote as we've seen in convention before, just because delegates are chosen does not mean that's how they're voted the convention. And so this is one of the things he made the decision. There will be an open, transparent and fair process going forward as the DNC has said. I think Kamala Harris is going to win that as we see people continue to rally around her build support. And I think you're going to see Democrats have momentum and energy going into the fall.",
