    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78130.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and look, I wish Democrats were that organized. But it really is something, it was both certainly as a member of Congress. I discussed it with my colleague, I discussed it with leadership. I take no joy in the idea that Joe Biden stepped aside to clear the path to make sure that Democrats have a chance to beat Donald Trump in the fall. But, you know, for me, it's something that I had been saying privately for a long time. And the decision only was whether to say it publicly. I say privately, you know, somebody stopped me in the grocery store and asked me where I think I'd tell them. It wasn't like some, you know, back room type thing. Anybody who asked me, I told them how I felt and how, what the numbers were showing and how things were playing out. And so one of the things that led me to my decision was we've got a town hall telephone town hall come up this week where people can call into, I knew this was going to come up. And I thought it was important for me to tell people what I thought and why I thought it.",
