    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78130.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "At the end of the day, this is the president's decision. And the president is the one to best know whether he can do the job, whether he can get the job. And I did not think the president in all the polling, in a polling across congressional districts, across other things, I didn't see the president with, I thought his chances of winning were so low and the stakes were so high that we probably needed to do something different. Use of sports analogy, it was time to make an adjustment. And that to me is really what it's about. And I think now too, I think you see passive agreement from the White House. You've watched this longer than I have. It's not often that politicians that I thought John Meacham this morning quoted a politician from Tennessee where he said the only cure for political ambition is embalming fluid.",
