  {
    "episode_id": 78130,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78130.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "I don't think it's unfair. I don't think it's unfair at all to say, let's see the president, let's see the president, let's see the president, let's see the photo or the president. From my experiences at the White House, coming to Congress. And I would just say, I'd never met a sitting president of the United States until I got elected to Congress. But whenever you are at the White House, or whenever you are around the president, even if it's in something that is quote unquote closed to the press, there are photographers there. There are people who are taking pictures of him all the time. I am confident there are pictures that are being taken of him today. And so if they're being released, I don't know the inside out of that. and have not been paying attention to that today. But those, I don't think it's unfair at all to ask for pictures of video. And I think he's also said he's going to address the country this week on it, which is important to do.",
